-- title:
--   Structural pairs of a product: $(\Gamma_1\times\Gamma_2,k_1\times k_2)$ is structural, and such pairs are cofinal among the structural pairs of $G_1\times G_2$
-- statement:
--   **Structural pairs of a product group** (auxiliary lemma for the proof of Lemma D.1.8.1(1)): products of structural pairs are structural, and they are cofinal among the structural pairs of the product.
--
--   Let $G_1$, $G_2$ be Hausdorff locally compact abelian groups (written multiplicatively). Recall (Definitions D.1.4.1, D.1.4.5 and D.1.5.1) that a subgroup $H$ of a locally compact abelian group $G$ is *compactly generated* if it is generated by a compact subset $U\subseteq H$ that is a neighbourhood of $1$ in $H$; that a subgroup $k$ of $G$ is *good* if $k$ is closed and its annihilator
--   $$k^\perp=\{\chi\in\widehat G:\ \chi(x)=1\ \text{for all }x\in k\}$$
--   is an open compactly generated subgroup of the Pontryagin dual $\widehat G$; and that a pair $(\Gamma,k)$ of subgroups of $G$ is *structural* if $\Gamma$ is open and compactly generated, $k$ is good, and $k\subseteq\Gamma$.
--
--   **Statement.**
--   1. If $(\Gamma_1,k_1)$ is a structural pair of $G_1$ and $(\Gamma_2,k_2)$ is a structural pair of $G_2$, then $(\Gamma_1\times\Gamma_2,\ k_1\times k_2)$ is a structural pair of $G_1\times G_2$.
--   2. For every structural pair $(\Gamma,k)$ of $G_1\times G_2$ there are a structural pair $(\Gamma_1,k_1)$ of $G_1$ and a structural pair $(\Gamma_2,k_2)$ of $G_2$ such that
--   $$\Gamma\subseteq\Gamma_1\times\Gamma_2\qquad\text{and}\qquad k_1\times k_2\subseteq k .$$
--
--   The Schwartz–Bruhat space $\mathcal S(G)$ is the inductive limit of its stages $\mathcal S(k,\Gamma)$ along the order $(\Gamma,k)\le(\Gamma',k')\iff\Gamma\subseteq\Gamma'$ and $k'\subseteq k$ on structural pairs (Definition D.1.5.3). The lemma says that the product pairs form a cofinal family of structural pairs of $G_1\times G_2$, so that $\mathcal S(G_1\times G_2)$ is the inductive limit of the stages of product pairs; this is the group-theoretic input of the proof of the kernel theorem $\mathcal S(G_1)\,\overline\otimes\,\mathcal S(G_2)\cong\mathcal S(G_1\times G_2)$ (Lemma D.1.8.1(1)).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The notions are the platform definitions `IsStructuralPair`, `IsGoodSubgroup`, `IsCompactlyGeneratedSubgroup` and `annihilator` of `MasulloGRH_SchwartzBruhat`; products of subgroups are `Subgroup.prod`. The dual of $G_1\times G_2$ is `PontryaginDual (G₁ × G₂)`; no identification with $\widehat G_1\times\widehat G_2$ is built into the statement.
-- source:
--   A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes, draft of 20 November 2026, https://math216.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/the-music-of-the-primes.pdf, p. 778, Lemma D.1.8.1(1); auxiliary lemma for the proof of Lemma D.1.8.1(1) (child of MasulloGRH.schwartzBruhat_prod_stages_isCompletedProjTensor): structural pairs of a product group (Definition D.1.5.1, p. 760)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MasulloGRH_SchwartzBruhat

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace MasulloGRH

theorem isStructuralPair_prod_and_le_prod
    (G₁ G₂ : Type*) [CommGroup G₁] [TopologicalSpace G₁] [IsTopologicalGroup G₁] [T2Space G₁]
    [LocallyCompactSpace G₁] [CommGroup G₂] [TopologicalSpace G₂] [IsTopologicalGroup G₂]
    [T2Space G₂] [LocallyCompactSpace G₂] :
    (∀ (Γ₁ k₁ : Subgroup G₁) (Γ₂ k₂ : Subgroup G₂), IsStructuralPair Γ₁ k₁ →
        IsStructuralPair Γ₂ k₂ → IsStructuralPair (Γ₁.prod Γ₂) (k₁.prod k₂)) ∧
    ∀ Γ k : Subgroup (G₁ × G₂), IsStructuralPair Γ k →
      ∃ (Γ₁ k₁ : Subgroup G₁) (Γ₂ k₂ : Subgroup G₂), IsStructuralPair Γ₁ k₁ ∧
        IsStructuralPair Γ₂ k₂ ∧ Γ ≤ Γ₁.prod Γ₂ ∧ k₁.prod k₂ ≤ k := by sorry

end MasulloGRH
